      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "xv5og2dyxnf7lxy",
                "text": "Changes in Amounts of Solids and Pure Liquids"
              }
            ],
            "id": "f3bqvudtqchtwt3",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Recall that a heterogeneous equilibrium is a system in which reactants and products are found in two or more phases. The phases may be any combination of solid, liquid, or gas phases and solutions. When dealing with these equilibria, remember that pure solids and pure liquids do not appear in equilibrium constant expressions. Therefore, changing amounts of pure solids or pure liquids in a reaction at equilibrium will have no effect on the equilibrium position."
              }
            ],
            "id": "zsm6vlwhzdwe78d",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
